{
  "note": "Gold answers for the fetchable lane: for each question, table(s) that genuinely answer it. Unlike data/benchmark_questions.json, which scores ranking against Data.norge catalogue records, this scores whether the right *retrievable* resource is found -- the v1 goal. Candidates were pooled from every retrieval method (search_report, semantic, resource index) and then checked against the registry directly, so the labels are not bounded by what any one retriever surfaced; several answers here were found by searching titles after every retriever missed them. `expected` lists ids judged to answer the question; any one of them counts as a hit. `expected: []` means the registry holds no table that answers it -- a coverage finding, not a retrieval failure, and those questions are excluded from recall. Labels are author-judged from table titles, which is the main limitation: a title can mislead, and no cell was fetched to confirm. Labels for agriculture, fisheries, forestry and foreign trade were widened after an audit: the originals named niche cuts (organic-only, Sami-only, salmon export) while the plain subject tables were left out, so correct retrievals scored as misses. Widened because those tables answer the question, not because a retriever returned them -- the distinction matters, since adopting whatever was returned would make the benchmark circular. ADDED 2026-09-14: a089–a099 cover dairy deliveries, nature-protection areas, Oslo kommune statbank population, and Norges Bank policy rate / exchange rates. Labels from published titles; dairy 2025, Oslo BEF008, Norges Bank IR/EXR, and naturvern layer were confirmed by live fetches. Dairy expected lists every year-card of the same Landbruksdirektoratet series (2013–2025), not only 2025 — each answers national milk delivered to dairies. Oslo questions name the Oslo statbank series, not SSB kommunetabeller that also contain Oslo as a region. CORRECTED 2026-10-21 (a047): `hva er gjennomsnittsalderen i Tromsø` was labelled with 07459 and 11342. The registry's own record of what those tables publish says 07459 publishes the measure `Personer` and 11342 publishes `Areal (km²)` and `Befolkning per 1.1.`; neither publishes an average age. Answering from them would mean computing a mean from a distribution, which this system is built not to do. 13536 publishes the measures `Gjennomsnittsalder` and `Medianalder` for kommuner, fylker og hele landet, and was added for that reason -- judged from the measures the table publishes, not from any retriever's output. The other labels are kept: they are about the same population and may answer related questions. This correction can only raise the number, so it is recorded with the before and after in GAPS.md. CORRECTED 2026-10-21 (a025): `foretak etter organisasjonsform` was labelled with 13702, 08076 and 09028, which publish `Nye foretak` and `Nyetablerte føretak` -- newly established enterprises, a narrower subject than the question. 14001 publishes the measure `Talet på føretak` with an `organisasjonsform` dimension, which is the question itself. Candidates were enumerated from the registry's index of published measures and dimensions, not from any retriever's output, and 14001 was taken as the plain subject table; 14002 and 14003 publish the same measure with næring added and were left out as breakdowns. This is the same error pattern as the 2026 widening of the agriculture, fisheries and foreign-trade labels: the original named a niche cut and the plain subject table was omitted. It can only raise the number, so before and after are both in GAPS.md. a035, a049 and a058 were audited the same way and left alone: their labels publish the measure the question asks for and are not wrong, so widening them would move the number without correcting anything.",
